--
N5008 [class.static.data]/4, [expr.unary.op]/3: `&unique_typeinfo<T>::id'
is the address of the static data member (an object, even though it is
constexpr and usable in constant expressions); each specialization's
member is a distinct object ([basic.compound]/3).  The front end replaces
the constexpr member by its value and reports "address_of error: '0' not
an lvalue", dropping the function.  libc++'s std::any identifies types
this way (`__get_fallback_typeid', any:175), dropped in cpp17_libcxx_any;
test_libcxx.desc is that program and forbids only that drop.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept both programs.  Pre-existing (fails on bin52).
